  "5. Multinational Capital & Managerial Availability: The corporate balance sheet's ability to deploy millions in capital expenditure and station experienced expatriate executives abroad.",
  "The algorithm processes these variables through structured decision logic: (a) If regulatory mandates forbid 100% foreign ownership, Wholly-Owned FDI is disqualified, forcing an Equity Joint Venture or Licensing; (b) If IP sensitivity is extreme (e.g. advanced biotechnology or proprietary source code), Licensing is disqualified to prevent technology theft; (c) If capital availability is severely constrained, Exporting or Licensing is selected; and (d) If market potential is massive, risk is low, and IP sensitivity is high, Wholly-Owned FDI is selected to maximize long-term shareholder value.",
  "Running this simulation generates a robust, defensible market entry roadmap for executive leadership and the Board of Directors.",
  "As you review the code and worked example for Interactive Code Simulation: Cross-Border Entry Mode Decision Matrix in Python, notice how each variable represents a concrete operational lever rather than an abstract formula. When maintained shifts relative to local, the immediate ripple effect appears in mandates and ultimately reshapes brand. Keeping that cause-and-effect chain clear in your mind makes it much easier to explain your conclusions to stakeholders who need clear, plain-language justification.",
