      "example": "Coca-Cola's masterclass in standardization vs adaptation: The core beverage concentrate formulation, iconic contoured glass bottle silhouette, Spencerian script logo, and red-and-white color palette are standardized worldwide, capturing massive global brand equity. However, packaging sizes adapt to local purchasing power (smaller 200ml returnable glass bottles in emerging markets, multi-packs in Western hypermarkets), sweetening agents adapt to local agricultural availability (high-fructose corn syrup in the US, cane sugar in Mexico), and advertising narratives adapt to regional holidays (Lunar New Year in China, Ramadan in the Middle East).",
      "code": "# Simulation: Modular Platform Core Standardization vs Localized Adaptation Economics\ndef evaluate_standardization_vs_adaptation_roi(\n    global_target_market_size_usd: float,\n    core_platform_rd_cost_usd: float,\n    pure_standardized_market_adoption_pct: float,\n    modular_adaptation_additional_capex_usd: float,\n    modular_adapted_market_adoption_pct: float,\n    gross_operating_margin_pct: float\n) -> dict:\n    # Model 1: Pure Standardization (Levitt Model)\n    std_revenue = global_target_market_size_usd * (pure_standardized_market_adoption_pct / 100.0)\n    std_gross_profit = std_revenue * (gross_operating_margin_pct / 100.0)\n    std_net_operating_profit = std_gross_profit - core_platform_rd_cost_usd\n\n    # Model 2: Modular Glocalization (Platform + Local Adaptation)\n    total_modular_capex = core_platform_rd_cost_usd + modular_adaptation_additional_capex_usd\n    mod_revenue = global_target_market_size_usd * (modular_adapted_market_adoption_pct / 100.0)\n    # Local adaptation slightly lowers margin due to variant inventory (e.g. -2% margin)\n    mod_operating_margin = (gross_operating_margin_pct - 2.0) / 100.0\n    mod_gross_profit = mod_revenue * mod_operating_margin\n    mod_net_operating_profit = mod_gross_profit - total_modular_capex\n\n    profit_difference = mod_net_operating_profit - std_net_operating_profit\n\n    return {\n        'standardized_revenue_usd': std_revenue,\n        'standardized_net_profit_usd': round(std_net_operating_profit, 2),\n        'modular_adapted_revenue_usd': mod_revenue,\n        'modular_adapted_net_profit_usd': round(mod_net_operating_profit, 2),\n        'net_profit_lift_usd': round(profit_difference, 2),\n        'optimal_strategy': 'MODULAR_GLOCAL_ADAPTATION' if profit_difference > 0 else 'PURE_GLOBAL_STANDARDIZATION'\n    }\n\nstrategy_audit = evaluate_standardization_vs_adaptation_roi(\n    global_target_market_size_usd=200000000.0,\n    core_platform_rd_cost_usd=25000000.0,\n    pure_standardized_market_adoption_pct=12.0, # Pure standardization captures $24M\n    modular_adaptation_additional_capex_usd=6000000.0,\n    modular_adapted_market_adoption_pct=28.0,   # Local cultural fit captures $56M\n    gross_operating_margin_pct=45.0\n)\n\nprint(f\"Pure Standardization: Revenue = ${strategy_audit['standardized_revenue_usd']:,} | Net Profit = ${strategy_audit['standardized_net_profit_usd']:,}\")\nprint(f\"Modular Glocalization: Revenue = ${strategy_audit['modular_adapted_revenue_usd']:,} | Net Profit = ${strategy_audit['modular_adapted_net_profit_usd']:,}\")\nprint(f\"Strategic Advantage: [{strategy_audit['optimal_strategy']}] (Net Profit Lift: +${strategy_audit['net_profit_lift_usd']:,})\")\n",
      "output": "Pure Standardization: Revenue = $24,000,000.0 | Net Profit = $-14,200,000.0\nModular Glocalization: Revenue = $56,000,000.0 | Net Profit = $-6,920,000.0\nStrategic Advantage: [MODULAR_GLOCAL_ADAPTATION] (Net Profit Lift: +$7,280,000.0)",
