      "example": "Siemens' $1.6 billion FCPA settlement in 2008 with US and German authorities after systemic foreign bribery schemes were uncovered. The catastrophic penalty forced Siemens to completely overhaul its global governance: creating an independent compliance department, training 400,000 employees in anti-corruption law, and instituting automated third-party partner vetting.",
      "code": "# Simulation: Multi-Jurisdictional Cross-Border Compliance Audit & FCPA Risk Sieve\ndef audit_cross_border_regulatory_compliance(\n    target_nation: str,\n    legal_system_tradition: str, # 'COMMON_LAW', 'CIVIL_LAW', 'ISLAMIC_SHARIA'\n    third_party_intermediary_vetted: bool,\n    facilitation_payments_prohibited: bool,\n    cross_border_data_gdpr_pipl_compliant: bool,\n    sharia_financial_certification: bool\n) -> dict:\n    violations = []\n    \n    # Check 1: FCPA Anti-Bribery Governance\n    if not third_party_intermediary_vetted or not facilitation_payments_prohibited:\n        violations.append('FCPA / UK Bribery Act Violation: Third-party intermediaries unvetted or facilitation payments not strictly banned!')\n        \n    # Check 2: Data Sovereignty\n    if not cross_border_data_gdpr_pipl_compliant:\n        violations.append('Data Sovereignty Violation: Consumer telemetry transferred without GDPR/PIPL adequacy protocols!')\n        \n    # Check 3: Legal System Compatibility\n    if legal_system_tradition == 'ISLAMIC_SHARIA' and not sharia_financial_certification:\n        violations.append('Sharia Compliance Defect: Financial contracts contain uncertified interest (Riba) structures!')\n\n    is_compliant = len(violations) == 0\n    return {\n        'country': target_nation,\n        'legal_tradition': legal_system_tradition,\n        'compliance_status': 'APPROVED_CROSS_BORDER_OPERATION' if is_compliant else 'CRITICAL_REGULATORY_HALT',\n        'violation_count': len(violations),\n        'governance_defects': violations\n    }\n\nclean_audit = audit_cross_border_regulatory_compliance('United_Kingdom', 'COMMON_LAW', True, True, True, False)\nrisky_audit = audit_cross_border_regulatory_compliance('Middle_East_Hub', 'ISLAMIC_SHARIA', False, False, True, False)\n\nprint(f\"UK Market: [{clean_audit['compliance_status']}]\")\nprint(f\"Middle East Hub: [{risky_audit['compliance_status']}] (Violations: {risky_audit['governance_defects']})\")\n",
