      "title": "Phase 2: Behavioral Pricing Architecture & Asymmetric Decoy Deployment",
      "say": [
        "Having streamlined ACB's brand portfolio from twenty-eight sprawling labels down to twelve fortified strategic assets, you turn your attention to Phase Two: overhauling the corporate pricing and packaging architecture. In ACB's premium nutritional wellness division, the flagship offering, 'NutriCore Supreme' (a daily functional health supplement), is currently sold through direct-to-consumer e-commerce and retail pharmacy channels using a primitive, linear pricing structure: a standard 30-day bottle sold for $39.00. However, customer conversion rates have plateaued, and Average Order Value (AOV) is stagnating.",
        "To revitalize revenue velocity without resorting to gross-margin-depleting price discounts, you apply the cognitive principles of Kahneman and Tversky's Prospect Theory, Thaler's Choice Architecture, and Ariely's Asymmetric Decoy Effect. You recognize that consumers do not evaluate $39.00 in a cognitive vacuum; their purchasing decisions are governed by reference points, transaction utility, and comparative choice framing.",
        "You architect a revolutionary Three-Tier Behavioral Choice Architecture for NutriCore Supreme: Tier 1 (Entry/Core): Standard 30-Day Supply (Single Bottle) priced at $49.00. Tier 2 (Asymmetric Decoy): 60-Day Supply (Two Bottles) priced at $89.00. Tier 3 (Target Premium Bundle): 90-Day Complete Clinical Protocol (Three Bottles PLUS a complimentary precision diagnostic vitamin blood-test kit and digital tracking app subscription) priced at $99.00.",
        "Analyze the cognitive geometry of this behavioral architecture: Tier 2 is an Asymmetrically Dominated Decoy. For a customer evaluating Tier 2 ($89.00 for 60 days) against Tier 3 ($99.00 for 90 days plus diagnostic kit and app), Tier 3 appears as an overwhelming, irresistible bargain. For an incremental ten dollars, the consumer receives an additional thirty-day supply of supplements (worth $49.00 at list price) plus sixty dollars worth of digital diagnostic value. The presence of the $89.00 decoy completely eliminates buyer decision paralysis: it provides an immediate, frictionless comparative justification for System 1, channeling customer volume directly into the high-margin Tier 3 protocol.",
        "Furthermore, you apply Prospect Theory's gain-segregation and loss-integration principles to the checkout experience. Rather than displaying an itemized shipping fee ($8.50) and handling surcharge ($3.50) that trigger painful neural loss aversion in the insular cortex, you integrate all logistics into the advertised package price ('All-Inclusive Free Express Shipping'). Simultaneously, you segregate promotional gains by unbundling bonus perks into distinct, sequential visual gifts during checkout ('Bonus 1: Personalized Nutrition Guide ($25 Value) FREE; Bonus 2: 24/7 Dietitian Chat ($40 Value) FREE').",
        "To optimize subscription retention, you leverage the Default Effect and Mental Accounting. You establish the 90-day subscription auto-renewal as the pre-selected default option, framed as 'The VIP Wellness Membership—Only $1.10 Per Day.' This reframes the transaction out of the high-stakes annual capital expenditure mental account and into the frictionless daily pocket-change mental account, dramatically lowering churn rates across initial buyer cohorts.",
        "You test this behavioral pricing engine in a large-scale, randomized controlled trial across two hundred thousand prospective digital buyers. The results validate your behavioral model with staggering statistical power: the proportion of buyers selecting the premium bundle surges from thirty-two percent to seventy-six percent, driving a thirty-four percent expansion in Average Order Value and expanding division gross contribution margin by $38.4 million annually.",
        "To maintain regulatory compliance and consumer goodwill, you ensure that cancellation protocols remain entirely transparent and frictionless. Subscribers can pause, alter shipment frequency, or cancel with a single click, completely avoiding dark patterns while building deep, enduring brand loyalty that reinforces Customer Lifetime Value (CLV).",
        "Furthermore, behavioral choice architecture is continuously audited against ethical governance guidelines. Growth engineering teams utilize predictive telemetry to verify that customers who select the 90-day subscription protocol genuinely utilize and benefit from the diagnostic testing kits. By aligning pricing incentives with measurable customer health outcomes, ACB establishes an unassailable reputation for clinical integrity, driving organic word-of-mouth referrals and expanding subscription net revenue retention across all digital cohorts."
      ],
      "example": "When Williams-Sonoma introduced an expensive $429 breadmaker next to their existing $279 model that wasn't selling, sales of the $279 model nearly doubled. Consumers didn't know if $279 was fair until an expensive anchor made it look like a sensible compromise. ACB uses the same comparative framing.",
      "code": "def evaluate_acb_behavioral_pricing_uplift(\n    total_monthly_visitors: int,\n    conversion_rate_pre: float,\n    pre_price_single: float,\n    conversion_rate_post: float,\n    tier1_price: float,\n    tier2_decoy_price: float,\n    tier3_target_price: float,\n    post_choice_distribution: dict # {'Tier1': float, 'Tier2': float, 'Tier3': float}\n) -> dict:\n    # Pre-Turnaround Baseline\n    pre_buyers = int(total_monthly_visitors * conversion_rate_pre)\n    pre_monthly_revenue = pre_buyers * pre_price_single\n    pre_aov = pre_price_single\n    \n    # Post-Turnaround Behavioral Architecture\n    post_buyers = int(total_monthly_visitors * conversion_rate_post)\n    units_t1 = int(post_buyers * post_choice_distribution['Tier1'])\n    units_t2 = int(post_buyers * post_choice_distribution['Tier2'])\n    units_t3 = int(post_buyers * post_choice_distribution['Tier3'])\n    \n    post_monthly_revenue = (units_t1 * tier1_price) + (units_t2 * tier2_decoy_price) + (units_t3 * tier3_target_price)\n    post_aov = post_monthly_revenue / post_buyers if post_buyers > 0 else 0.0\n    \n    monthly_revenue_uplift = post_monthly_revenue - pre_monthly_revenue\n    annual_revenue_uplift = monthly_revenue_uplift * 12.0\n    aov_expansion_pct = ((post_aov - pre_aov) / pre_aov) * 100.0\n    \n    return {\n        'pre_monthly_revenue_m': round(pre_monthly_revenue / 1e6, 2),\n        'post_monthly_revenue_m': round(post_monthly_revenue / 1e6, 2),\n        'pre_aov_usd': round(pre_aov, 2),\n        'post_aov_usd': round(post_aov, 2),\n        'aov_expansion_pct': round(aov_expansion_pct, 1),\n        'annual_revenue_uplift_m': round(annual_revenue_uplift / 1e6, 2),\n        'target_tier3_adoption_share_pct': round(post_choice_distribution['Tier3'] * 100.0, 1)\n    }\n\n# Simulation of Phase 2 Behavioral Pricing Rollout\np2 = evaluate_acb_behavioral_pricing_uplift(\n    total_monthly_visitors=350000,\n    conversion_rate_pre=0.032, # 3.2% conversion\n    pre_price_single=39.0,\n    conversion_rate_post=0.038, # Increased conversion due to cognitive ease\n    tier1_price=49.0,\n    tier2_decoy_price=89.0,\n    tier3_target_price=99.0,\n    post_choice_distribution={'Tier1': 0.18, 'Tier2': 0.06, 'Tier3': 0.76} # 76% choose Target!\n)\n\nprint(f\"Pre-Turnaround Monthly Revenue: ${p2['pre_monthly_revenue_m']}M | Baseline AOV: ${p2['pre_aov_usd']}\")\nprint(f\"Post-Turnaround Monthly Revenue: ${p2['post_monthly_revenue_m']}M | New AOV: ${p2['post_aov_usd']}\")\nprint(f\"Average Order Value (AOV) Expansion: +{p2['aov_expansion_pct']}%\")\nprint(f\"Target Premium Bundle Adoption Rate: {p2['target_tier3_adoption_share_pct']}%\")\nprint(f\"Annualized Top-Line Revenue Expansion: +${p2['annual_revenue_uplift_m']}M\")",
      "output": "Pre-Turnaround Monthly Revenue: $0.44M | Baseline AOV: $39.0\nPost-Turnaround Monthly Revenue: $1.19M | New AOV: $89.4\nAverage Order Value (AOV) Expansion: +129.2%\nTarget Premium Bundle Adoption Rate: 76.0%\nAnnualized Top-Line Revenue Expansion: +$9.03M",
