      "title": "Phase 1: IMC Touchpoint Synergy, Attribution Architecture & Launch Budget Optimization",
      "say": [
        "You assume the role of Chief Global Commercial Officer (CGCO) at AuraHealth Technologies (AHT), a $2.4B multinational biometric healthcare and continuous medical monitoring corporation headquartered in Zurich, Switzerland. AHT is preparing the global commercial launch of its flagship device: the AuraVital Pro. The AuraVital Pro is an advanced medical-grade biosensing wearable paired with an AI-powered predictive metabolic telehealth ecosystem (AuraCare Cloud). Unlike consumer fitness trackers, the AuraVital Pro holds FDA Class II clearance in the United States and CE Medical Device Regulation (MDR) certification in the European Union, positioning it at the premium intersection of lifestyle elegance and clinical diagnostic precision. The enterprise supervisory board has allocated a substantial $45,000,000 international launch budget across North America, Western Europe, and Asia-Pacific. Your primary strategic directive in Phase 1 is to architect an integrated marketing communications campaign that maximizes customer acquisition while preventing message dissonance, audience burnout, and attribution misallocation.",
        "Your first task is structuring the $45M capital allocation across the PESO Framework (Paid, Earned, Shared, and Owned Media). Rather than allowing media agencies to dump 80% of the budget into uncoordinated programmatic digital advertising, you establish an integrated media mix designed for compounding returns. Paid Media ($24.0M) is allocated across Connected TV (CTV) narrative films, high-impact medical journal print inserts, programmatic digital video, and sponsored search. Earned Media ($6.0M) funds international clinical public relations, medical symposium keynotes, peer-reviewed clinical trial publications in The New England Journal of Medicine, and investigative press briefings with tier-one media (The Wall Street Journal, Financial Times, Der Spiegel). Shared Media ($5.0M) activates co-creations with vetted cardiologists, marathon runners, and medical micro-influencers. Crucially, Owned Media ($10.0M) finances the creation of the AuraHealth Digital Health Academy, clinical white papers, and the high-conversion AuraCare direct portal.",
        "To prevent audience burnout and budget incineration across programmatic digital channels, you implement Centralized Cross-Channel Frequency Capping via an enterprise Demand-Side Platform (DSP) identity graph. Guided by Herbert Krugman's Three-Hit Theory and modern wear-out models, you establish a global frequency cap of 5 exposures per unique household across all digital channels within any rolling 7-day window. Furthermore, you deploy automated bid shading algorithms that scale bids down by 80% when impressions occur within 4 hours of a prior exposure, enforcing healthy cognitive spacing. To defeat creative wear-out, you commission Dynamic Creative Optimization (DCO) engines with three rotating narrative sequels: Phase A focuses on 'Curiosity and Clinical Distinction' (What is AuraVital Pro?); Phase B demonstrates 'Empirical Diagnostic Accuracy' (How does continuous metabolic telemetry save lives?); and Phase C delivers 'Physician Endorsement and Risk-Free Onboarding' (The call to action).",
        "You segment the target international audience into two distinct behavioral cohorts: Clinical High-Risk Patients (individuals managing pre-diabetes, hypertension, or arrhythmia seeking diagnostic security) and Proactive High-Performance Executives (biohackers, endurance athletes, and corporate leaders seeking peak metabolic performance). For Clinical Patients, communications follow the Central Route of the Elaboration Likelihood Model (ELM), delivering dense empirical charts, cardiologist testimonials, and clinical trial efficacy statistics. For High-Performance Executives, communications leverage the Peripheral Route, featuring sleek titanium aesthetics, minimalist typography, and high-energy cinematic vignettes depicting executive vitality.",
        "Finally, you completely reject Last-Touch Attribution, which historically misled AHT into over-allocating capital to branded search engines that were merely capturing existing demand. You deploy an Algorithmic Multi-Touch Attribution (MTA) engine based on Cooperative Game Theory Shapley Value Attribution. The Shapley model evaluates user journey coalitions across CTV, Medical PR, Cardiology Influencers, and Direct Search. The algorithm proves that Earned Medical PR and Clinical Influencers generate 41.5% of total incremental conversion causality, despite rarely being the last click before purchase. By reallocating $7.2M away from bottom-funnel search into clinical earned authority and owned content, you lower AHT's blended Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC) by 28.4% while generating 14,200 additional high-LTV enterprise subscriptions.",
        "To ensure unified cross-border orchestration, you establish a centralized Global Marketing Command Center. All regional creative agencies must submit campaign assets through an automated brand compliance portal that scans copy for regulatory claim integrity (ensuring no unauthorized medical claims violate FDA 510(k) or EU MDR statutes). By synchronizing flighting schedules and unifying message encoding across broadcast, digital, and print channels, AHT eliminates semantic noise and establishes undeniable global category leadership from day one."
      ],
      "example": "During pre-launch modeling, AHT's Last-Touch model claimed Google Search was responsible for 72% of conversions. Switching to Shapley Value attribution revealed Search had an incremental causality score of only 21%, while Earned Medical PR had a causality score of 44%. Reallocating $7.2M from Search to Medical Symposiums and Cardiology White Papers expanded qualified medical leads by 38%.",
      "code": "def optimize_aura_imc_launch_allocation(\n    total_budget_usd: float,\n    peso_splits: dict[str, float], # channel -> pct of budget\n    baseline_cac_last_touch: float,\n    shapley_attribution_weights: dict[str, float] # true incremental weights\n) -> dict:\n    channel_budgets = {ch: total_budget_usd * pct for ch, pct in peso_splits.items()}\n    \n    # Calculate organic subsidy lift from earned, shared, owned\n    # High earned/owned reduces blended CAC\n    earned_owned_share = peso_splits.get('Earned', 0.0) + peso_splits.get('Owned', 0.0)\n    cac_reduction_factor = 1.0 - (earned_owned_share * 0.55)\n    optimized_blended_cac = baseline_cac_last_touch * cac_reduction_factor\n    \n    projected_total_acquisitions = int(total_budget_usd / optimized_blended_cac)\n    acquisitions_under_last_touch = int(total_budget_usd / baseline_cac_last_touch)\n    incremental_customers = projected_total_acquisitions - acquisitions_under_last_touch\n    \n    return {\n        'channel_budgets_usd': {ch: round(b, 2) for ch, b in channel_budgets.items()},\n        'baseline_cac': baseline_cac_last_touch,\n        'optimized_blended_cac': round(optimized_blended_cac, 2),\n        'projected_acquisitions': projected_total_acquisitions,\n        'incremental_acquisitions_gained': incremental_customers\n    }\n\n# Test Case: $45M Global Launch Budget for AuraVital Pro\nlaunch_audit = optimize_aura_imc_launch_allocation(\n    total_budget_usd=45000000.0,\n    peso_splits={'Paid': 0.533, 'Earned': 0.133, 'Shared': 0.111, 'Owned': 0.223},\n    baseline_cac_last_touch=380.0,\n    shapley_attribution_weights={'Paid': 0.35, 'Earned': 0.38, 'Shared': 0.12, 'Owned': 0.15}\n)\n\nprint(f\"Optimized Blended CAC: ${launch_audit['optimized_blended_cac']:.2f} (vs Baseline: ${launch_audit['baseline_cac']:.2f})\")\nprint(f\"Projected Device & Service Subscriptions: {launch_audit['projected_acquisitions']:,}\")\nprint(f\"Incremental Customers Unlocked via Shapley IMC: {launch_audit['incremental_acquisitions_gained']:,}\")",
      "output": "Optimized Blended CAC: $305.60 (vs Baseline: $380.00)\nProjected Device & Service Subscriptions: 147,251\nIncremental Customers Unlocked via Shapley IMC: 28,830",
